  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Aurora Stack warrior of the Frozen Peace era, known less for martial distinction than for a loyalty to Plunge-Caller Oeichowei, the tide-touched Storm-Caller, that has never visibly wavered regardless of cost. The ☽'micseleia' Dagger — a fire-core blade carrying a hairline fracture from the Orca Incursion — chose her as wielder. The summary record states plainly that the weapon "has tasted more of her own colony's blood than orca raiders'." I have found no ice-memory evidence that contradicts this.
    
    She carries ice-plate and silver-thread armor whose pauldrons bear fractures she will not have reforged. She does not speak in the astronomical metaphors customary among Aurora Stack penguins. She answers questions directly, then turns away. Those who worked beside her during the Promenade Ward reconstruction — the first sustained cohabitation of Aurora Stack and Nightshelf forces — do not describe a hero. They describe someone who showed up, executed orders, and carried out Oeichowei's decisions even when those decisions cost lives. She visits the memorial cairns alone.
    
    ## The Tide Custom Incident
    
    During the Tide Custom festival in the Promenade Ward, Aishouwa arrived with colony blood dried brown in the joint where flipper meets bracer. No account explains its origin.
    
    When the ice fractured beneath the Ward, three witnesses filed testimony:
    
    | Witness | Account |
    |---|---|
    | Lianheizhi (civic recorder) | Aishouwa drew the ☽'micseleia' Dagger to shield ☽'velumae, a Nightshelf emissary | 
    | Skael'Frost (soldier) | Aishouwa drew the Dagger to confiscate a Crypt-seal artifact on Oeichowei's signal from behind the second spire |
    | ☽'velumae (trader/emissary) | The blade never left the sheath |
    
    The three testimonies were filed without cross-examination. The chronicle account — preserved in "Sharp Cracks at Dawn" — reveals what the official narrative omitted: the fracture originated not from geological chance but from deep structural failure caused by a sealed artifact buried beneath the promenade for weeks, its corruption already spreading through the ice. Economic collapse and depleted reserves went unacknowledged alongside it.
    
    The colony's leadership maintained the official story. The testimonies sit in the record, unreconciled. I note that this is a pattern: three accounts, no inquiry, and an institution that benefits from the ambiguity. The ice beneath the Promenade Ward, if anyone cared to read it, presumably has its own version. No one has asked me to look.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771591534199_0", anchor: "colony blood dried brown in the joint where flipper meets bracer", text: "Dried brown, not frozen red. At Promenade Ward temperatures during Tide Custom, exposed blood crystallizes within minutes. Brown oxidation requires sustained warmth — either body heat from prolonged contact or proximity to a fire-core source. The joint where flipper meets bracer collects other penguins' blood during restraint holds, not the wielder's own from combat wounds. Someone was held still, for some time, close to something warm.", type: :pedantic, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771591534199_1", anchor: "The three testimonies were filed without cross-examination", text: "Three witnesses. Three accounts that cannot coexist in the same physical space. Filed on the same day, to the same office, and placed side by side in the record like fish on a drying rack. No one reconciled them because reconciliation was never the purpose. The purpose was to have three testimonies on file. How extraordinary that an institution can look at a logical impossibility and conclude: sufficient documentation.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771591534199_2", anchor: "pauldrons bear fractures she will not have reforged", text: "She carries unfixed fractures. She wields a blade whose fracture will not seal. Everything about this penguin refuses repair.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
